From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:11:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: power the internal DCP down for any
 deep sleep

A deep sleep needs the display coprocessor and its domains off: its
display DARTs refuse the sleep while they're on. So a plain suspend with
appledrm.power_gate_ms at 0 was always refused. Power them down for a
deep sleep whatever the parameter says, and leave it deciding only the
power-down after a blank and the one before suspend-to-idle.

[dylan: hand-ported onto the firmware-driven sleep check this tree has
 (iomfb_m4_suspend_firmware(), dcp-m4-sleep.h) in place of the upstream
 iomfb_m4_suspend() branch: the check now takes the power-down as enabled
 for such a sleep. The J604's default power_gate_ms is 5000, so nothing
 changes at the defaults; suspend-to-idle and blanking are unchanged.]

Hand-ported from Aurora commit f8046eacf47c ("drm/apple: m4: power the
internal DCP down for any deep sleep").

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 821f6e59ec..6874b209f4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@ static const struct kernel_param_ops power_gate_ms_ops = {
 
 module_param_cb(power_gate_ms, &power_gate_ms_ops, &power_gate_ms, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(power_gate_ms,
-		 "J713, J604: power the display coprocessor and its domains down after this many ms blanked, and before system sleep (0: never; default: the machine's, J604 5000, J713/J715 0; at most 600000; applies from the next blank)");
+		 "J713, J604: power the display coprocessor and its domains down after this many ms blanked, and before system sleep (0: only before a deep sleep; default: the machine's, J604 5000, J713/J715 0; at most 600000; applies from the next blank)");
 
 /*
  * DCP CPU control and status, in the coprocessor's ASC block. The idle bit
@@ -7334,7 +7334,12 @@ int iomfb_m4_suspend_firmware(struct apple_dcp *owner)
 		.failed = READ_ONCE(dcp->error) != 0,
 		.gated = dcp->gated,
 		.gate_capable = dcp->gate_capable,
-		.gate_enabled = READ_ONCE(power_gate_ms) != 0,
+		/*
+		 * A sleep that powers the SoC down needs the power-down whatever
+		 * power_gate_ms says: the parameter decides only the power-down
+		 * after a blank and before suspend-to-idle.
+		 */
+		.gate_enabled = true,
 		.scanning = dcp->active_fb || dcp->active_frame.dva,
 		.display_off = dcp->display_off && !dcp->powered_off,
 	};
-- 
